WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.400
Up to 200 million containers may still leech PFOA, which has no safe level in drinking water. This is Omni View Top World News, Episode 26. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. The Environmental Protection Agency has rewritten its own page on two of the most dangerous PFS chemicals. The Guardian reports the old line said PFOA manufacture and imports were finished in the United States. The new line says companies may still produce, import, and use some.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:33.780
Cancer researchers class PFOA as carcinogenic to people and PFOS as possibly carcinogenic.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.280
Houston firm Enhance is still turning out those containers and tests have found PFOA leaching

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.180
into what they hold.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:45.700
Former agency scientist Kyla Bennett, now with public employees for environmental responsibility,

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.780
